// S-957 (W5-11 U10d2/t2, §2.1, §2.5, §4.5): a block comment between the `?` of a bound and its name, on the line of the name,
// is the E0020 of the block comment (§2.1) first (S-957: "the block comment's own E0020 is first"), and the line break
// after the `?` is not reported with it: one unit reports one error (P-01). Its one candidate writes a line comment
// (`// c`) and keeps the tokens and the line breaks, so the break after the `?` is still there after it and is the
// error of the next round (`leaves`: the E0020 of the `?`, at the place it stood). The main position is the start of the
// block comment. This file passes without S-957 as far as the first error goes: the comment was the first error before it
// too, and it must stay so after it. A file with one unit, so that the candidate is the one of the comment.

pub fn f[T: ?
  /* c */ Dup](x: T) -> U32 {   //~ E0020 @3
